<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Douce I, Countess of Provence</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1090–<a href="/years/1127">1127</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Douce of Provence</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Douce I was Countess of Provence and heiress of its first comital dynasty. Her marriage to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramon-berenguer-iii-of-barcelona">Ramon Berenguer III of Barcelona</a> in 1112 brought Provence to the counts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barcelona">Barcelona</a>, whose junior line ruled it until 1245. Her rights were contested by the counts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toulouse">Toulouse</a>, leading to a partition of Provence between the two houses in 1125.</p></div>
